WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.694
LinkedIn serves thirty

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:02.991
million ML features

00:00:02.803 --> 00:00:03.569
a second

00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:05.442
LinkedIn built Venice

00:00:05.336 --> 00:00:06.927
an open-source distributed

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:07.541
platform

00:00:07.659 --> 00:00:08.685
to separate data

00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:09.970
production from online

00:00:09.782 --> 00:00:10.583
consumption

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:11.986
with batch and

00:00:11.798 --> 00:00:13.119
streaming ingestion

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:15.245
Imagine a recommendation

00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:16.543
platform making one

00:00:16.354 --> 00:00:17.958
hundred thousand predictions

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.477
a second

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.833
each needing three

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:21.106
hundred feature values

00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:22.026
which adds up

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:22.958
to thirty million

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.960
values a second

00:00:24.494 --> 00:00:26.156
Venice gives low-latency

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.524
access to materialized

00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:28.161
information

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:29.423
so serving machine

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:30.425
learning data becomes

00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:31.675
an infrastructure problem

00:00:31.522 --> 00:00:32.335
as big as

00:00:32.147 --> 00:00:32.866
training

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.404
Full story on

00:00:34.215 --> 00:00:35.111
the dashboard
